From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: soc_button_array: allow ARM64 again

7.3 made INPUT_SOC_BUTTON_ARRAY depend on X86 when it moved the driver to
GPIOLIB_LEGACY. The driver has nothing x86-only in it (the Intel SoC checks
in <linux/platform_data/x86/soc.h> are stubbed out elsewhere), and ACPI
arm64 machines use it: on the Radxa Orion O6N (CIX P1) the power button is
an ACPI0011 Generic Buttons device, and without this driver it neither
works nor wakes the board from s2idle.

Kettle Linux (Radxa Orion O6N).
---
 drivers/input/misc/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig b/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig
index 169768e3d..eea6d95c5 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig
@@ -904,7 +904,7 @@ config INPUT_IDEAPAD_SLIDEBAR
 config INPUT_SOC_BUTTON_ARRAY
 	tristate "Windows-compatible SoC Button Array"
 	depends on KEYBOARD_GPIO && ACPI
-	depends on X86
+	depends on X86 || ARM64
 	depends on GPIOLIB
 	select GPIOLIB_LEGACY
 	help
